## 4. Component Deep-Dive {#4-components}

### 4A. n8n — The Orchestration Brain

**Why n8n and not pure code?**
- Visual workflow builder — non-developers on your team can see and understand the pipeline.
- Built-in retry, error handling, and webhook triggers.
- Native HTTP Request nodes to call your Portal-Service APIs.
- Easy to add new scraping sources without touching code.
- Self-hosted (free, runs on your own server alongside Portal-Service).

**n8n Setup:**
```bash
# Self-hosted n8n via Docker (runs alongside your Portal-Service)
docker run -d --name n8n \
  -p 5678:5678 \
  -v n8n_data:/home/node/.n8n \
  --restart unless-stopped \
  n8nio/n8n
```

### 4B. Scraping Worker — Separate Node.js Microservice

The scraper runs as a **standalone Node.js service** (not inside n8n) because:
- Playwright/Crawlee needs a full Chromium browser, which is too heavy for n8n's execution model.
- It can run on a separate machine or container with more RAM.
- n8n triggers it via HTTP webhook and receives results back.

```
Portal-Service (Port 3004) ← Your existing backend
Scraping-Worker (Port 4000) ← New microservice
n8n            (Port 5678) ← Orchestration
Redis          (Port 6379) ← Already running (shared queue)
```

### 4C. AI Extraction — Gemini 2.0 Flash

The AI extraction prompt is **the single most important piece of the system**. Here's the exact prompt template:

```
You are a real estate data extraction engine for JustFlip.in.
Extract property details from the following webpage content.
Return ONLY valid JSON matching this exact schema.
Rules:
- If a field is not explicitly stated on the page, return null. NEVER guess.
- RERA numbers must be copied exactly as shown. If not found, return null.
- Prices must be converted to pure integers in the smallest currency unit (e.g., ₹1.25 Cr = 12500000).
- Unit types should be normalized to: "1BHK", "2BHK", "3BHK", "4BHK", "5BHK", "Studio", "Penthouse", "Villa", "Plot", "Duplex".
- Amenity names should be common English names (e.g., "Swimming Pool", "Gymnasium", "24x7 Security").
- Property type must be one of: "apartment", "villa", "plot", "penthouse", "row house", "farmhouse".

Required JSON Schema:
{
  "name": "string",
  "builderName": "string",
  "description": "string (2-3 sentences about the project)",
  "type": "apartment|villa|plot|penthouse|row house|farmhouse",
  "rera": "string or null",
  "city": "string",
  "zone": "string (area/direction, e.g., East, West, North, South)",
  "location": "string (locality/neighborhood name)",
  "towers": "integer or null",
  "floors": "string or null (e.g., 'G+14')",
  "totalUnits": "integer or null",
  "landParcel": "string or null (e.g., '5.2 Acres')",
  "possessionStatus": "string (e.g., 'Under Construction', 'Ready to Move', 'Pre-Launch')",
  "possessionDate": "ISO date string or null",
  "coordinates": { "lat": number, "lng": number } or null,
  "units": [
    {
      "type": "string (e.g., '2BHK')",
      "currency": "INR|AED|USD",
      "minPrice": integer or null,
      "maxPrice": integer or null,
      "interiorArea": integer or null (in sq.ft)
    }
  ],
  "amenities": ["string"],
  "images": [
    { "type": "image", "title": "banner|logo|floor plan|other", "url": "string", "alt": "string" }
  ]
}
```

