## 10. Failure Handling & Recovery {#10-failure-handling}

### Every Failure Scenario Mapped:

| Stage | Failure | Detection | Recovery | Human Action Needed? |
|:---|:---|:---|:---|:---|
| **Scraping** | Target site is down or blocks IP | HTTP 403/503/timeout | n8n retries 3x with 30s backoff. If still fails, log error and skip URL. Retry in next cron cycle. | ❌ No |
| **Scraping** | Anti-bot CAPTCHA triggered | Page content is empty / CAPTCHA detection | Switch proxy. If persists, mark URL as `captcha_blocked` and alert team on Slack. | ⚠️ Maybe (switch proxy provider) |
| **Scraping** | Page layout changed (selectors broken) | AI extraction returns mostly null fields | Confidence score drops below 0.3 → auto-skip staging. Alert on Slack: "Scraper may be broken for domain X". | ✅ Yes (update scraper) |
| **AI Extraction** | Gemini API rate limit (429) | HTTP 429 response | n8n retries with exponential backoff (5s, 15s, 45s). | ❌ No |
| **AI Extraction** | Gemini returns invalid/hallucinated JSON | JSON parse fails or schema validation fails | Discard this extraction. Log the raw response for debugging. Move to next property. | ❌ No |
| **AI Extraction** | Gemini returns null for critical fields (name, city) | Post-extraction validation check | Do NOT stage this record. Log as `extraction_failed`. | ❌ No |
| **Entity Resolution** | Builder not found in JustFlip DB | API returns empty result | Stage the record WITH `validation_warnings: ["builder_not_found"]` and `resolved_builder_id: null`. Reviewer must create the builder first or map manually. | ✅ Yes |
| **Entity Resolution** | City/Location not found | API returns empty result | Same as above. Flag as `location_not_found`. Reviewer maps it. | ✅ Yes |
| **Staging Write** | PostgreSQL connection error | Write throws error | n8n retries 3x. If still fails, send Slack alert with full payload so nothing is lost. | ⚠️ Maybe (DB issue) |
| **Deduplication** | False positive duplicate | Fuzzy match is too aggressive | Reviewer sees the `matched_project_id` and can override: "This is NOT a duplicate, create as new." | ✅ Yes (that's why humans review) |
| **Production Push** | `create-from-dashboard` returns 400 error | API error response | Update `staged_projects` with `status: 'failed'`, `push_error: error.message`. Reviewer can fix the data and retry. | ✅ Yes |
| **Production Push** | `create-from-dashboard` returns 500 / timeout | Server error | n8n retries 2x. If still fails, mark as `failed` with error. The staging record is preserved — nothing is lost. | ✅ Yes (investigate server) |
| **Update Push** | `PUT /project/:id` returns 404 (project deleted between scrape and review) | API 404 response | Convert the staged record from `action_type: 'update'` to `action_type: 'create'`. Notify reviewer: "Original project no longer exists — create as new?" | ✅ Yes |
| **Update Push** | `PUT /project/:id` returns 400 (validation error on updated fields) | API 400 response | Same as create failure — mark `status: 'failed'`, preserve payload. Reviewer fixes and retries. | ✅ Yes |
| **Update Push** | Update succeeds but new `approval: 'pending'` blocks live display longer than expected | Project disappears from live site during re-approval | Expected behavior by design. Alert the team via Slack so they can fast-track the re-approval. | ✅ Yes (fast-track approval) |
| **Production Push** | Duplicate name error from API | API returns "Project with this name already exists" | Mark staged record as `duplicate`. Notify reviewer. | ✅ Yes |
| **Image Upload** | CDN upload fails | HTTP error during image transfer | Store original image URLs in staging. Reviewer can manually trigger re-upload. Images are not blocking — project can be created without them. | ⚠️ Maybe |

### The Golden Rule of Failure Handling:
> **No data is ever lost.** Every scraped payload is persisted in `staged_projects` before any production operation is attempted. If production push fails, the staging record remains intact with the error message, and the reviewer can fix and retry.

### Dead Letter Queue (DLQ)
For records that fail production push 3+ times:
- Move to `status: 'failed'` with full error context.
- Send a daily digest to Slack: *"5 staged projects failed to push. [Review Failed Items]"*
- These stay in the staging table until manually resolved — they never get auto-deleted.

