## Summary: Why This Design Works for JustFlip

| Concern | How It's Handled |
|:---|:---|
| **"Bad data on the live site"** | Impossible. Data goes through staging → human review → explicit approval before touching production. Projects are created with `status: inactive`, `approval: pending`. |
| **"What if the AI hallucinates?"** | The reviewer sees the original webpage screenshot side-by-side. Any hallucinated field is immediately visible. |
| **"What if scraping breaks?"** | Failures are logged and retried. Staging records preserve everything. Daily Slack digests flag persistent issues. |
| **"What if a push to production fails?"** | The staging record stays with `status: failed` and the error message. Reviewer can fix and retry. Nothing is lost. |
| **"What if a builder/location doesn't exist yet?"** | Flagged as a validation warning. Reviewer creates the missing entity first, then approves. |
| **"Audit trail?"** | Every staged record tracks: source URL, screenshot, who reviewed it, when, what was changed, and the resulting `projectId`. |
| **"Can we add more sources later?"** | Yes. Add a new Crawlee scraper and a new n8n trigger. The extraction → staging → review → push pipeline is source-agnostic. |
